## Engine & IDE standards (UE 5.8 / Rider)

- **`FGameplayTag` over raw `FName`** for puzzle networks, quest IDs, combat channels — compile-time validation kills typo-induced silent no-ops.
- **StateTree** for quest progression, NPC behaviour, dialogue branching. **World Partition Data Layers** to switch lighting/cinematic passes without duplicating maps. **CommonUI `CommonActivatableWidget`** + input routing for focus, gamepad legends, back-button stacks. **`TRACE_CPUPROFILER_EVENT_SCOPE`** around rhythm maths and tick loops. **`UEditorValidatorSubsystem`** rules for asset safety on save.
- **Rider:** Code Vision lenses read Blueprint counts/CDO overrides without the editor; `TObjectPtr<T>` for GC-tracked members; IWYU pruning against unity-build pollution; RiderLink runs automation tests live; `qodana.yaml` `QDJB` profile for leaks/missing reflection.
- **Shader module `Source/MelodiaShader`** needs `LoadingPhase: PostConfigInit` (a module registering a virtual shader directory must load before the shader compiler) and a **closed-editor** `Build.bat` pass to add/rename — Live Coding cannot register new reflected types.

### Melodia MCP / Monolith

- **Single editor lock.** All editor-mutating tools (Monolith, T3D injectors, PIE runners) serialize through one holder. Never competing MCP instances on one graph or level.
- **Discover before declaring impossible.** Query Monolith's 1330+ actions (`monolith_discover`) before claiming a capability can't be automated.
- **Safe reflection over Python wrapping.** Never inspect user-defined enums (e.g. `D_DamageType`) via `load_blueprint_class()`; use Monolith C++ reflection (`get_cdo_properties`, `get_graph_data`).

